ys  out that way then how do you break that  loop now this is where Tom King kind of  just I wouldn't say screws the pooch but  certainly takes the story in the  direction where it seems to kind of take  away from the impact of everything  because then what you end up having is  boosters all new charms up and says hey  just run to the future and just get a  cone of yourself and like kill the clone  bring it back drop the body off and then  you're fine you don't have to kill  yourself five days in the future and so  like that's it it's such an easy way out  to be honest it's such an easy way out  but that's kind of the funny thing is  because if you look at heroes in crisis  as a traditional superhero story then  yes that ending sucks and it ruins the  whole thing but if you look at it for  what it's supposed to be which is a  deconstruction of Wally West it's not  about the steps that while he takes in  order to to win the day it's about  what's going on with Wally how does he  view the world if you look at it through  those eyes the entire nature of the  story changes and I think that's where a  lot of people struggled I think a lot of  people kind of went into this because DC  built it that way so you really can't  fault them for it but a lot of people  went into this like it's a great big  huge event and it's a it's a huge story  and like all kinds of crazy things are  gonna happen DC didn't really build it  as a deconstruction of Wally  DC built it build it as like this is the  next big event you know and it's like  okay and then you get into and you  realize this doesn't quite work the way  it's supposed to now the thing about  this this is kind of the cool moment the  thing about this is that Wally kind of  sits down and says okay so I've done  this right like I went to the Future I  grabbed a clone I dropped it off I  killed him and that's the body they  discover done and done the recursive  time loop disclosed things can move  forward  there's still the question of what  happens to wall-e what goes on now  because while they kill people and then  he lied about it the frame boosts our  golden Harley Quinn and then he forced  Superman's hand to dump a bunch of  information that really probably  shouldn't been dumped in the first place  you know so what we're talking about  here is a guy who engaged in murder and  espionage so like what do you do with a  guy like that well of course  Wally ends up being taken to prison and  just kind of dropped off in a Cell now  it's sort of left open-ended by it by  Tom King and the sense of like Wally's  there but we don't really know what  comes next  I imagine that question will be answered  in Joshua Williamson's flash right like  Joshua waves will probably pick up from  that and and go from there either that  or Williamson will ignore it in its  entirety and it'll be like heroes and  crisis never happened and that'll just  be the end of it I don't know how you  treat the story like it never happened  if it was confined strictly to Wally and  he basically managed to open the time  loop and close it and no one knew about  it then sure you could just kind of  shoot this under the rug and say here's  a crisis never happened at all you're  talking about and call it a day but like  the confessions of the superheroes being  blasted out to the world you can't  really sweep that under the rug there's  no real areal like coming back from that  but at the end of the day again heroes  in crisis you know like I said if you  look at it for what it is right like the  way it was designed to be viewed then  it's a beautifully done story but the  issue is that a lot of folks are kind of  let in under the belief that it was a  big crisis crossover kind of Grand  Poobah event and and that was it so I  don't know I mean I'm I'm curious what  do you guys think I'm curious what your  opinions are because I'm sure they're  gonna vary I'm sure they're gonna be  people who are gonna be like here is a  crisis sucked and they're gonna be  people who are like heroes a crisis was  amazing so I'm curious what your all's  response is what you're all sought is I  enjoyed it but again I think the ending  kind of took away from what could have  been a great story even with it being a  deconstruction of wall-e but nonetheless  let me do you guys think if you are new  here to come this explain it make sure  you guys have the sub button to become  part of the Rob core if you guys enjoyed  this video then make sure you drop a  like and yeah I will catch you all later  purse  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

